/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  MageRide Driver — iOS · C088 driver-ios-dashboard-dispatch. தமிழ்.

  SCOPE. Cluster 3 only: SCR-DI-010 the Mode C dashboard, SCR-DI-011 the Mode A/B Start/End Journey
  dashboard, SCR-DI-013 Directional Travel, SCR-DI-014 the fifteen-second dispatch takeover,
  SCR-DI-015 the active ride and SCR-DI-036 the Menu tab.

  KEYS ARE C070'S. Same key names and the same translations as
  `apps/driver-android/src/main/res/values…/strings.xml`, so a divergence between the two driver
  apps is a diff rather than an archaeology exercise. `%1$s` becomes `%1$@`, which is the only
  systematic difference — see cluster 2's note above.

  THREE KEYS ARE NEW HERE, and each is something this platform draws and Android does not.
  `offer_countdown` is the ring's VoiceOver label — the Android twin's ring is a
  `CircularProgressIndicator` with the seconds as a sibling `Text`, which a screen reader already
  reads, while this one is a drawn shape and announces itself. `ride_call_unavailable` is the CallKit
  refusal: a `tel:` URL on iOS *places* the call, so dialling over an existing one hangs it up, where
  Android's `ACTION_DIAL` only opens the dialler. `menu_driver` is SCR-DI-036's card label, which the
  Android drawer takes from `app_name`.

  NOT HERE. `home_daily_fee_*` carries no `Rs` of its own and `L3` is not a string at all — both are
  data, not copy (`MoneyFormat.prefix`, `DashboardLabels.level`). SCR-DI-035's buffered-samples card
  is C093's on this platform and its copy comes with it.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

